A partial: the one way a prompt learns the repository's settings (D-SETTINGS-LINE,
#392). Prompts never read `project.json`, the personal `config.json` or the
machine manifest for a value this line carries — `resolve-settings.cjs` folds all
three, and `tests/guards/no-config-read.test.ts` holds every compiled prompt to it.

Each command host that has a consumer imports this file itself, as an ALIAS import
(a selective import deep-clones this module's scope into every define of the
importer), and expands `settings_resolve()` exactly once, immediately before the
earliest of its consumers: its decisions load or gate, its compliance lens, its
publication gate, its knowledge write-back Step 1, or a Skim spawn that takes
`LEARNING`. The gate partials import nothing from here: their text refers to the
settings line resolved above and keeps each gate's own condition inside its own step.

The block stays a per-root procedure: "reusing a line this run already resolved for
the same root". A consumer whose `{root}` may differ from the first-resolved root
names that root and says its line is the one for that root, resolved by the block
above when this run has not yet resolved it. The guard counts textual invocations,
not runtime calls.

The accepted shape below is `SETTINGS_LINE_RE` written out, and the fallback is
`SETTINGS_FAIL_CLOSED_LINE`, both exported by `resolve-settings.cjs`;
`tests/commands/settings-partial.test.ts` pins both to the script.

@define settings_resolve():
**Resolve the settings line** once per worktree root, reusing a line this run already resolved for the same root. `{root}` is the worktree the values are for — the repository root when the run has one worktree:

```bash
node "$HOME/.devflow/scripts/resolve-settings.cjs" "{root}" 2>/dev/null; echo "exit=$?"
```

Accept the output only when it is exactly two lines: `exit=0` last and, before it, one line of the form `TRACKER=<github|jira|linear> TRACKER_SOURCE=<project|personal|machine|default> TRACKER_WARN=<none|mismatch|invalid> SITE=<none|https://<host>> KEY=<none|<key>> REVIEW_PUBLICATION=<off|auto|full> COMPLIANCE=<off|generic|<id>[,<id>…]> MEMORY=<on|off> LEARNING=<on|off> KNOWLEDGE=<on|off>` — these fields, in this order, nothing else, where `<host>` is a lowercase dotted host name alone, `<key>` is 2–10 of `A-Z`, `0-9` and `_` starting with a letter, and each `<id>` is one of `gdpr`, `hipaa`, `pci-dss`, `soc2`, `iso-27001`, `sox`. **Anything else** (a non-zero exit, no line, extra text, or a missing, reordered or unlisted field or value) ⇒ use `TRACKER=github TRACKER_SOURCE=default TRACKER_WARN=invalid SITE=none KEY=none REVIEW_PUBLICATION=off COMPLIANCE=generic MEMORY=on LEARNING=on KNOWLEDGE=off` instead.

The accepted line is the only source of these values: the script alone folds the committed `.devflow/project.json`, the personal `.devflow/config.json` and the machine manifest.
@end

@export settings_resolve
